# Machine-specific paths for scripts/start-stack.sh. Copy to ~/.cloudsentinel-stack.env (or point
# CS_STACK_ENV at another file) and adjust. KEY=VALUE per line; ~ and $HOME are expanded. The file is
# parsed, never executed. Environment variables override it; unset keys use the defaults in the script
# (paths relative to the checkout the script runs from).
#
# Model files and Python venvs are gitignored, so they usually live in the checkout where they were built
# and not in every clone. Example for a machine where ml-sast v3 was built in ~/cs-sast, ml-dast v4 in
# ~/cs-dast, and the backend .env is in ~/CloudSentinel:
#
# CS_SAST_MODEL_DIR=~/cs-sast/services-ml/ml-sast/models/release_v3
# CS_SAST_VENV=~/cs-sast/services-ml/ml-sast/.venv
# CS_DAST_MODEL_DIR=~/cs-dast/services-ml/ml-dast/models/release_v4
# CS_DAST_VENV=~/cs-dast/services-ml/ml-dast/.venv
# CS_BACKEND_DIR=~/CloudSentinel/backend
# CS_BACKEND_ENV=~/CloudSentinel/backend/.env
# CS_HF_HOME=/mnt/d/cs-data/hf-cache
# CS_TMPDIR=/mnt/d/cs-data/tmp
# CS_LOG_DIR=~/cs-logs
# MINIKUBE_PROFILE=minikube
#
# Code directories (default: the checkout the script is in). Set them only to run the services from
# another checkout:
# CS_SAST_DIR=~/cs-sast
# CS_DAST_DIR=~/cs-dast
